@@ -1,3 +1,18 @@
+pve-firewall (6.0.6+supermox3) trixie; urgency=medium
+
+  * PVE/Firewall.pm: let SuperMox's own cluster traffic through the host firewall.
+    Upstream's corosync rule covers only "-p udp --dport 5404:5405", the single
+    port the legacy net-socket transport used; knet, the transport PVE::Corosync
+    writes, binds mcastport (5405 in PVE's config) and the 7 ports above it, so
+    the range is widened to 5404:5412. The management ipset, the per-pair overlay
+    rules and the localnet output rules also carry "-p tcp --dport 8743"
+    (supermox-joind) and "-p udp --dport 51820" (the wg0 tunnel's WireGuard
+    traffic). With the host firewall on and policy_in DROP, none of that traffic
+    was accepted, so a joined node stopped answering CORE_REQ and join traffic
+    and the cluster never converged.
+
+ -- SuperMox <noreply@supermox.me>  Fri, 06 Nov 2026 02:03:46 -0800
+
 pve-firewall (6.0.6+supermox2) trixie; urgency=medium
 
